## Objective Statement

### Formal Objective

The Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) shall perceive the operating environment by acquiring, maintaining, and updating relevant observations of external, internal, human, and operational conditions required to support subsequent interpretation, reasoning, and adaptive decision-making.

---

### Objective Intent

Establish the system's capability to acquire and maintain reliable observations of its operating environment as the foundation for all subsequent adaptive processing.

---

### Success Criteria

This objective is considered satisfied when the system demonstrates the ability to:

- Acquire relevant observations from the operating environment.
- Detect changes in observable conditions.
- Maintain an up-to-date representation of observed information.
- Provide observations suitable for downstream interpretation.
- Continue perception within defined engineering constraints.

---

### Engineering Constraints

- The objective shall remain solution-independent.
- The objective shall not prescribe sensing technologies, hardware, or algorithms.
- The objective shall describe observation only and shall not include interpretation, reasoning, or decision-making.
- All derived perception objectives shall remain traceable to this objective.

---

### Assumptions

- Relevant information exists within the operating environment and can be observed.
- Subsequent objectives will interpret and act upon the observations provided by this objective.
